### 6\. Create Dockerfile

Create a new file named exactly:

`Dockerfile`

Paste:

```dockerfile

FROM node:20-alpine

WORKDIR /app

COPY package*.json ./

RUN npm install --omit=dev

COPY . .

EXPOSE 3000

CMD ["node", "index.js"]
```

Understand the commands:

| Command | Meaning                        |
| ------- | ------------------------------ |
| FROM    | Selects Node.js base image     |
| WORKDIR | Sets application directory     |
| COPY    | Copies project files           |
| RUN     | Executes installation commands |
| EXPOSE  | Documents application port     |
| CMD     | Starts the Node.js application |

Create another file called `.dockerignore`:

```text
node_modules
.git
.env
```

This prevents unnecessary files from being copied into the Docker image.

