### Part G – Automate the pipeline (important!)

This is the actual automation part.

Until now, we manually built and pushed Docker images. Now we'll make GitHub do that automatically whenever we push code.

### 18\. Add GitHub Actions workflow

Inside your project, create this folder structure:

```text
program-6/
│
└── .github/
    └── workflows/
        └── docker-build.yml
```

Create the file `docker-build.yml`.

Paste this complete code:

```yaml

name: Docker Automated Build Pipeline

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main

jobs:
  build-and-push:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    permissions:
      contents: read
      packages: write

    steps:
      - name: Checkout Source Code
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Login to Docker Hub
        uses: docker/login-action@v3
        with:
          username: ${{ secrets.DOCKERHUB_USERNAME }}
          password: ${{ secrets.DOCKERHUB_TOKEN }}

      - name: Login to GHCR
        uses: docker/login-action@v3
        with:
          registry: ghcr.io
          username: ${{ github.actor }}
          password: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}

      - name: Build Docker Image
        run: |
          docker build -t program-6 .

      - name: Push to Docker Hub
        run: |
          docker tag program-6 ${{ secrets.DOCKERHUB_USERNAME }}/program-6:latest
          docker push ${{ secrets.DOCKERHUB_USERNAME }}/program-6:latest

      - name: Push to GHCR
        run: |
          docker tag program-6 ghcr.io/${{ github.repository_owner }}/program-6:latest
          docker push ghcr.io/${{ github.repository_owner }}/program-6:latest
```

This workflow performs six operations:

| Stage | Operation                |
| ----- | ------------------------ |
| 1     | Checkout source code     |
| 2     | Login to Docker Hub      |
| 3     | Login to GHCR            |
| 4     | Build Docker image       |
| 5     | Push image to Docker Hub |
| 6     | Push image to GHCR       |

